2. Geographic & Network Source
Network Graph: OpenStreetMap (OSM) real road network topology.
Bounding Box: Beeramguda, Hyderabad (17.505°N, 78.287°E to 17.530°N, 78.312°E).
OSM Source File: data/geo_v2/beeramguda_roads.osm.json (Real Overpass API road response preserving all OSM way IDs, nodes, lanes, and one-way directions).
Vehicle Simulation: 1,000 active vehicles operating at 120-second (2-minute) temporal sliding window ticks.
3. Feature Contract & Variants
Geo V2 uses a 10-Feature Spatial Contract:

avg_speed_kmph: Average vehicle speed on road segment
speed_std_kmph: Standard deviation of speeds
vehicle_count: Active vehicle count on segment
occupancy: Segment density fraction
flow_rate_vph: Vehicles per hour flow rate
stopped_fraction: Fraction of stationary/stuck vehicles
hour_sin: Cyclic sine transform of time of day
hour_cos: Cyclic cosine transform of time of day
road_type_code: Encoded OSM road classification
lane_count / max_speed_kmph: Road physical capacity attributes
Extended Feature Sets:

history_current (22 features): Adds historical baseline speeds, trend deltas, and low-speed persistence.
history_spatial (29 features): Adds 1st-degree neighbor segment speeds, neighbor vehicle counts, and spatial delta features.
4. 8 Event Classes & Priority Rules
Deterministic label hierarchy for resolving concurrent events on the same segment: $$\text{road_block} \succ \text{flood} \succ \text{accident} \succ \text{construction} \succ \text{road_damage} \succ \text{diversion} \succ \text{congestion} \succ \text{normal}$$

